WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.180
South Korea is withdrawing more embassy staff from Ukraine after a prisoner of war disclosure dispute. This is Omni View, episode 211. Malaysia's opposition loses its registration, families prepare to return to a Cape Town neighborhood after apartheid era removals, and Alberta decides on Canada than markets, a progress watch, and understanding the issue. A Sharjay Daffer, the diplomat who runs an embassy when the ambassador is gone, will remain in Kiev with all consular staff.

00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:34.580
South Korea's Ministry of Foreign Affairs said to keep diplomatic communication open and

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.300
protect South Korean nationals.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.320
The ministry tied the extra pull out to Ukraine's disclosure of the transfer of two captured

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.860
North Korean soldiers without prior coordination.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:49.320
It said Kiev had not given a constructive response despite multiple channels of communication,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:53.700
and it pointed to ongoing security risks from airstrikes across Ukraine.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.900
Under South Korea's constitution, all North Koreans are considered citizens of the Republic

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.880
of Korea. Those who reach its territory and seek to defect are generally allowed to stay.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:09.660
From that legal ground, ministry spokesperson Park Dusun said the measure was taken to facilitate

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:15.240
an amicable resolution and restore trust between the two countries. That is the strongest case

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:20.880
soul puts forward. A calibrated protest meant to repair a relationship with a working embassy

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:26.200
channel left in place so the two governments can still talk. Ukraine has insisted that diplomacy

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:31.900
must prevail over emotions, and it described the situation as resolved. In Kiev's framing,

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:37.520
the matter belongs in the diplomatic channel, not in a cycle of public grievance, and an apology

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:42.780
has already been offered. The disclosure came from President Vladimir Zelensky at the United

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:48.380
Nations General Assembly earlier this month. That appearance prompted Seoul to recall its ambassador

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:53.920
and threaten further measures. Foreign Minister Cho Hyun noted that a Ukrainian message included

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:57.580
words of apology, but fell short of the level Seoul had sought.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.380
Cho Hyeon's own account concedes the apology language is there.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.100
The remaining gap, as Seoul describes it, is whether those words meet the standard it

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:06.700
asked for.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.620
Persistent airstrike threats had also complicated staff safety.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:17.697
The ministry said, Perikotan National, Malaysia's main opposition coalition, lost its legal

00:02:17.697 --> 00:02:22.317
registration at the registrar of societies, the official body that registers political

00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:26.917
organizations, 11 days before nominations for the Malacca state election.

00:02:27.657 --> 00:02:32.277
Accusations that Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim's government is using state powers to weaken

00:02:32.277 --> 00:02:35.117
rivals were reported by the South China Morning Post.

00:02:35.617 --> 00:02:40.237
For those critics, a registrar's decision this close to a state poll is not a technical

00:02:40.237 --> 00:02:40.637
cleanup.

00:02:41.197 --> 00:02:45.277
It is the state deciding whether the main opposition grouping can still appear as one

00:02:45.277 --> 00:02:46.977
force when voters see the ballot.

00:02:47.697 --> 00:02:52.177
Opposition figures have put particular weight on that timing, because the blocks elect

00:02:52.177 --> 00:02:55.837
electoral identity is now uncertain ahead of the November 14th vote.

00:02:56.477 --> 00:03:01.897
Perikatan National had been the main opposition grouping, losing registration directly affects

00:03:01.897 --> 00:03:06.437
its ability to field candidates under a single banner rather than as separate parties walking

00:03:06.437 --> 00:03:07.597
into the same contest.

00:03:08.277 --> 00:03:13.617
The coalition was already strained by a dispute between its Islamist component, P.A.S., and

00:03:13.617 --> 00:03:15.437
its estranged partner, Bersatu.

00:03:16.177 --> 00:03:20.017
Those internal fractures continue while the block fights to preserve its structure.

00:03:20.017 --> 00:03:26.117
The Registrar's Act and the PAS, Versatou Split, now sit on the table together, and nominations

00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:29.557
will show what banner, if any, the opposition can still use.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.940
Families displays from Bishop's Court during apartheid era forced removals are scheduled

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.780
to return under a cross subsidized housing development.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:43.460
All Africa reported that the project aims to restore land access lost six decades ago,

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.860
while incorporating mixed-income housing.

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:50.620
planning. The plan is meant to address historical restitution and current housing needs in the

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:56.780
Cape Town area at the same time. Restitution here is not only illegal finding, it is a construction

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:02.500
schedule that puts people back on land they were forced off. Ground up noted that the cross-subsidized

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:08.700
model will allow lower income families to benefit alongside market rate units. Lower income households

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:13.700
are not waiting for a separate later project. They are written into the same development as the

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:18.760
market rate homes that help pay for it. That mixes the concrete mechanism for reversing

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:25.302
one specific forced removal. The work is due for completion in 2028. Alberta rejected

00:04:25.302 --> 00:04:31.082
a proposal to begin a process toward independence, with 76% supporting continued membership

00:04:31.082 --> 00:04:36.102
in Canada. The Guardian noted the result as a clear victory for Prime Minister Mark Carney

00:04:36.102 --> 00:04:41.802
and supporters of national unity. The ballot was not a snap opinion poll. It was the first

00:04:41.802 --> 00:04:47.122
formal referendum effort on separation in the province, and it is now over. With more

00:04:47.122 --> 00:04:52.342
than 1.5 million votes counted, that effort ends. Unofficial results from elections

00:04:52.342 --> 00:04:58.442
Alberta showed close to 24% backing the separation process. That share confirms the decisive

00:04:58.442 --> 00:05:03.702
margin against the measure. The count stands as a recorded signal of how the province voted

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:09.991
on remaining in the federation. Luxury home sales fell approximately 17% in Dubai in the

00:05:09.991 --> 00:05:14.611
third quarter, compared with the previous year, according to researcher Night Frank, as

00:05:14.611 --> 00:05:15.911
the Iran war continued.

00:05:16.531 --> 00:05:20.931
Wealthy international buyers remained active, but at lower volumes than the prior peak.

00:05:21.691 --> 00:05:22.491
Bloomberg reported.

00:05:23.131 --> 00:05:27.931
Caution around the ongoing regional conflict is showing up in fewer deals, even though

00:05:27.931 --> 00:05:30.191
demand from some markets has not disappeared.

00:05:30.831 --> 00:05:35.711
Transaction counts dropped, yet average prices in the luxury segment held relatively steady.

00:05:35.711 --> 00:05:40.851
That pattern points to a selective pullback rather than a broad walkaway by buyers.

00:05:41.451 --> 00:05:46.211
The war's persistence has introduced measurable caution into high-value property decisions.

00:05:47.242 --> 00:05:51.902
U.S. investors increased acquisitions of German industrial and manufacturing companies

00:05:51.902 --> 00:05:52.462
last year.

00:05:52.982 --> 00:05:59.382
They completed 76 acquisitions and investments valued at about $29.5 billion, nearly

00:05:59.382 --> 00:06:01.122
double the 2022 total.

00:06:01.722 --> 00:06:02.742
Deutscheweller reported.

00:06:02.742 --> 00:06:08.602
Many family-owned German firms, the Middle Stand, Germany's specialized industrial backbone,

00:06:09.142 --> 00:06:12.942
are becoming targets as owners reach retirement age without successors.

00:06:13.462 --> 00:06:19.182
US buyers are drawn to specialized technical expertise and to customer relationships built over decades.

00:06:19.902 --> 00:06:26.662
As of August 2026, US investors had already reached $23.9 billion in such deals for the year,

00:06:27.182 --> 00:06:28.482
according to pitch book data.

00:06:28.482 --> 00:06:35.682
Notable transactions included the $5.4 billion sale of EBM-PAPST to Madison Air and

00:06:35.682 --> 00:06:38.362
Bain Capital's 51% stake in Everlands.

00:06:39.408 --> 00:06:44.888
Saudi Arabia is pushing in the right direction on cardiac care in Nigeria, opening a medical

00:06:44.888 --> 00:06:47.448
campaign for patients who need specialized treatment.

00:06:47.928 --> 00:06:53.548
The program is set to perform 108 cardiac procedures, including 28 open heart surgeries

00:06:53.888 --> 00:06:57.328
and 80 catheterization procedures, leadership reported.

00:06:58.148 --> 00:07:02.008
catheterization here is a diagnostic and treatment method that threads a thin

00:07:02.008 --> 00:07:06.508
tube into the heart and it sits alongside the open heart operations in the same

00:07:06.508 --> 00:07:11.288
campaign. The effort is a concrete piece of bilateral health cooperation at a

00:07:11.288 --> 00:07:15.348
time when many Nigerian patients face limited access to advanced cardiac

00:07:15.348 --> 00:07:20.488
treatment at home. It bundles surgical interventions and diagnostic catheterizations

00:07:20.488 --> 00:07:24.848
into one coordinated push with a published count that can be checked against what

00:07:24.848 --> 00:07:25.968
is actually delivered.

00:07:26.955 --> 00:07:32.035
Tariq Rahman visited Durgapuja pavilions in Bangladesh also today, as the government

00:07:32.035 --> 00:07:36.575
increased its grant for the Hindu festival from four crore to five crore Taka.

00:07:37.395 --> 00:07:43.035
Japan's MMX spacecraft began its journey to Phobos, a moon of Mars, to collect surface

00:07:43.035 --> 00:07:45.935
samples that may clarify how the solar system formed.

00:07:46.707 --> 00:07:51.607
You need to really understand embassy staffing during a dispute as a reversible signaling tool,

00:07:52.007 --> 00:07:54.107
not as a synonym for breaking relations.

00:07:54.107 --> 00:07:59.587
A great deal of coverage treats a smaller mission as a dramatic escalation, as if the flag

00:07:59.587 --> 00:08:00.667
has already come down.

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:06.287
In ordinary diplomatic practice, cutting staff is a routine, reversible signal that stops

00:08:06.287 --> 00:08:07.587
short of ending relations.

00:08:08.267 --> 00:08:13.347
When a host country's actions create friction, an unplanned disclosure of sensitive information

00:08:13.347 --> 00:08:14.767
is one classic trigger.

00:08:15.327 --> 00:08:18.587
The sending state can reduce personnel in order to show displeasure.

00:08:19.167 --> 00:08:21.007
It can do that without closing the post.

00:08:21.007 --> 00:08:26.007
The Standard Remaining Channel is a Charge de Faire, who runs the mission when there is

00:08:26.007 --> 00:08:27.307
no ambassador on site.

00:08:27.787 --> 00:08:31.787
That arrangement lets both governments keep talking without the public picture of a

00:08:31.787 --> 00:08:35.087
full ambassador still in residence, as if nothing had happened.

00:08:35.727 --> 00:08:37.987
The same tool has a practical safety use.

00:08:38.467 --> 00:08:42.787
In a dangerous capital, a smaller political staff simply puts fewer people in harm's

00:08:42.787 --> 00:08:48.227
way, while a consular section can still serve citizens who need passports, welfare help,

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:49.147
or a way home.

00:08:49.147 --> 00:08:52.667
Calibration is the design, not an accident of wording.

00:08:53.207 --> 00:08:54.607
A true rupture looks different.

00:08:55.147 --> 00:09:00.267
The embassy shuts, consular work stops, and nationals lose an official door to knock on.

00:09:00.827 --> 00:09:02.507
A protest drawdown looks like this.

00:09:02.907 --> 00:09:07.687
Fewer diplomats, a charge still listed, and citizen services still running.

00:09:08.187 --> 00:09:12.607
The common misunderstanding is to hear staff withdrawn and conclude relations ended.

00:09:13.187 --> 00:09:16.307
Those are different steps, and they are supposed to be different steps,

00:09:16.307 --> 00:09:19.147
so that a dispute can be marked without burning the file.

00:09:20.171 --> 00:09:24.111
Official foreign ministry briefings tend to keep that distinction in the precise nouns

00:09:24.111 --> 00:09:24.731
they use.

00:09:25.331 --> 00:09:30.551
Secondary accounts often condense those nouns into a single verb, pulled, withdrew, hit

00:09:30.551 --> 00:09:33.271
back, and the calibration falls out of the sentence.

00:09:34.376 --> 00:09:39.316
When a drawdown is in the news, look up whether a charge de fares is still named, and whether

00:09:39.316 --> 00:09:42.156
the consular section is still processing work for citizens.

00:09:42.156 --> 00:09:42.356
positions.

00:09:42.756 --> 00:09:46.996
Put an official ministry briefing beside a secondary news account of the same dispute

00:09:46.996 --> 00:09:49.296
and notice which words survive the cut.

00:09:49.816 --> 00:09:53.016
Remaining diplomat, consular desk, protest, rupture.

00:09:54.144 --> 00:09:59.104
Malacca nomination papers come due shortly, and that filing deadline is the next hard date

00:09:59.104 --> 00:10:01.704
for how Malaysia's opposition will appear on the ballot.

